/-
# Tests.AnchorsSha — D338 (V2): the SHA-NI pins, in a module of their own

Arm (A) of the 2026-10-10 kernel-cost fork, taken from the start (D338 prediction 5): these `decide` pins never enter
`Tests.Anchors`. They are a NEW unit, judged once against an absolute registration measured on its own machine
(`scripts/kernel_ceilings.txt`, `scripts/ku_delta_budget.txt`), and `Tests.Anchors` keeps its budget — D311's rule (one
test module per witness family), applied to a family that is all one probe.

The block between the markers is GENERATED by `hwprobe/mk_sha_anchors.py` (`--check` gates it byte for byte).

LANE. Personal lane, public sources only.
-/
import X86

namespace X86.Tests.Sha
open X86

/-! ## D338 (V2) — SHA256MSG1, SHA256MSG2 and SHA256RNDS2 against a processor's reading

⚠️ NONE OF THESE HAS A DIFFERENTIAL PARTNER: ACL2 x86isa refuses all three at every pre-state.  So the rows below — run
by `hwprobe/sha_probe.c` on a hosted runner's processor, derived from the SDM's rules by `hwprobe/mk_sha_rows.py`, whose
known-answer rows come from a textbook FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 checked against the published digests — are the only check of
this model's numbers for them, and every row is pinned.

The pre-state is the probe's (`hwprobe/sha_ops.S`): %xmm1 = DEST (SRC1, all 128 bits), %xmm2 = SRC2, the m128 at RBX
holds the same SRC2 (16-byte aligned, as a legacy-SSE m128 must be), %xmm0 = the row's `k` (SHA256RNDS2's implicit
operand), and the six arithmetic flags are the row's `f`.  A row agrees when the step did not refuse, %xmm1 is the row's
128 bits, %xmm2, the m128 and %xmm0 are unchanged, the six flags are exactly `f` — "Flags Affected: None" — and RIP moved
by the instruction's length. -/

/-- The six arithmetic flags of an RFLAGS image (CF PF AF ZF SF OF at bits 0 2 4 6 7 11); DF stays clear —
`Tests.Anchors`' `w1bFlags`, restated because that one is private to its module. -/
private def v2Flags (f : BitVec 64) : Flags :=
  ⟨f.getLsbD 0, f.getLsbD 2, f.getLsbD 4, f.getLsbD 6, f.getLsbD 7, f.getLsbD 11, false⟩

/-- The RFLAGS image of the flags this model keeps, at `flagFields`' positions (`Tests.Anchors`' `b0Rflags`). -/
private def v2Rflags (f : Flags) : BitVec 64 :=
  flagFields.foldl (fun acc r => acc ||| (if r.get f then (1 : BitVec 64) <<< r.bit else 0)) 0

/-- `sha_ops.S`'s pre-state, at RIP 0x400000 with the m128 SRC2 at 0x2000 (16-byte aligned). -/
private def v2Pre (a b k : BitVec 128) (f : BitVec 64) : Cpu :=
  (((({ regs := ({} : Regs).set .rbx 0x2000, flags := v2Flags f, mem := {}, rip := 0x400000,
        oracle := Oracle.zero } : Cpu).setXmm .x0 k).setXmm .x1 a).setXmm .x2 b).writeMem128 0x2000 b

private def v2Agrees (t : Cpu) (n : Nat) (b k : BitVec 128) (f : BitVec 64) (w : BitVec 128) : Bool :=
  t.ms.isNone && t.getXmm .x1 == w && t.getXmm .x2 == b && t.getXmm .x0 == k && t.readMem128 0x2000 == b
    && (v2Rflags t.flags &&& 0x8d5) == (f &&& 0x8d5) && t.rip == 0x400000 + BitVec.ofNat 64 n

